	"system": {
		"description": "<p>The reason for your exile provides you one of the following benefits:</p><p><strong>Criminal</strong></p><p>Your people were exiled as thieves and brigands. You gain advantage on Stealth Checks to hide in crowds or in manufactured environments such as starships or cities.</p><p><strong>Genetic</strong> </p><p>Your people were exiled due to genetic differences, whether through manipulation or evolution. Choose a heritage trait that keys off of an ability score or modifier, and then choose a different ability score or modifier for that trait. Alternatively, if you have a trait with a range or movement speed, you can increase it by 10ft or 5ft respectively.</p><p><strong>Political</strong></p><p>Your people were exiled over political disputes. When you make a Charisma check and roll a 5 or less you may instead treat the dice roll as a 10: this includes attack rolls and saving throws. Once you have used this ability you may not do so again until you take a short or long rest.</p><p><strong>Religious</strong></p><p>Your people’s faith resulted in your exile. Choose a Cleric Cantrip that you gain access to.</p><p><strong>Warfare</strong></p><p>Whether your people were a soldier caste thrown away when no longer needed or the losing side in a war, violence is the reason for your exile. You gain proficiency with three Weapons or Vehicles of your choosing.</p>",
